# Example for running Prisma against Railway Postgres **from your laptop** only.
#
# The public URL (Railway → Postgres → Connect → **Public Network**) is reachable
# from the internet. The private URL (`postgres.railway.internal`) is not.
#
# Usage:
# 1. Copy this file to `.env.railway-public` (git-ignored) or set DATABASE_URL only in your shell.
# 2. Paste your public connection string from Railway (host + port from "Public Network").
# 3. From `services/backend-api`, run migrations with that URL active, e.g.:
#      set DATABASE_URL=...   (PowerShell: $env:DATABASE_URL="...")
#      npx prisma migrate deploy && npx prisma generate
#    Or merge the line below into `.env` temporarily (do not commit).
#
# Do not commit real credentials. Do not use this URL as the runtime DATABASE_URL
# for your API service on Railway when the API and DB are in the same project
# (use the private/internal URL / ${{ Postgres.DATABASE_URL }} there instead).
#
# DATABASE_URL="postgresql://postgres:PASSWORD@HOST:PORT/railway?schema=public"
#
# Delete `.env.railway-public` when you are done migrating.
